<title>ITALY: EMU delay would need fresh treaty talks - Charette.</title>
<headline>EMU delay would need fresh treaty talks - Charette.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Any proposal to delay the start of Europe's economic and monetary union would mean renegotiating the Maastricht Treaty and such a process would end in disagreement, French Foreign Minister Herve de Charette said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;France will never propose it,&quot; de Charette told reporters at a meeting of European Union foreign ministers in Rome. &quot;If you open a renegotiation...there will be no agreement at all on anything,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
